---
import DocumentLayout from '../layouts/DocumentLayout.astro';
import { pages } from '../data/pages';
---

<DocumentLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="Practical terms for using these free, browser-based image utilities."
  eyebrow="UPDATED OCTOBER 27, 2026"
  metaTitle={pages.terms.metaTitle}
  metaDescription={pages.terms.metaDescription}
>
  <h2>Use of the toolkit</h2>
  <p>
    PixelTools provides general image-processing assistance. Only process files
    you are authorized to use, and comply with applicable laws and the rights of
    other people. You remain responsible for your input, output, publishing
    choices, and the requirements of any destination service.
  </p>
  <h2>Your images</h2>
  <p>
    You retain your rights in the images you choose and generate. Local
    processing does not grant this website a license to your selected images.
    Original files on your device are not overwritten. Review generated output,
    filenames, and available metadata before sharing it.
  </p>
  <h2>Technical limitations</h2>
  <p>
    Processing is subject to documented file, pixel, batch, runtime, and browser
    limits. Compression targets are goals rather than guarantees. Converting to
    a lossless pixel format does not restore previously lost detail. Social
    presets are reviewed suggestions or identified official recommendations, not
    a promise that every placement or account will accept the result.
  </p>
  <h2>Availability and accuracy</h2>
  <p>
    The utilities may contain errors or behave differently across browsers and
    devices. Validate important results independently. Availability and
    compatibility may change, and no continuous-service commitment is offered.
  </p>
  <h2>Responsibility</h2>
  <p>
    To the extent permitted by applicable law, the tools are provided as
    available without a warranty of fitness for a particular purpose. Nothing in
    these terms excludes rights or liabilities that cannot lawfully be excluded.
    Review the limitations on each tool page before relying on it in
    consequential work.
  </p>
  <h2>Updates and contact</h2>
  <p>
    Terms may be revised, with the current update date shown above. Operator
    identity, contact details, and any jurisdiction-specific provisions should
    be confirmed before a public launch. Read the{' '}
    <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>,{' '}
    <a href="/disclaimer">Disclaimer</a>, or{' '}
    <a href="/contact">contact information</a> for more context.
  </p>
</DocumentLayout>
